# Planner contracts (RFC-001)

Truth rule: if code and `docs/RFC-001-planner.md` disagree, update the RFC in the **same** change.

## Normative defaults (do not silently change)

| Constant               | Value                                                             |
| ---------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Peak road factor       | ×1.45 on Gojek / motorcycle / car / TJ — **not** KRL/MRT/LRT/walk |
| P80 (road/mix summary) | ≈ P50 × 1.4                                                       |
| Monthly cost           | `oneWayCost × 2 × WFO_days × 4.33`                                |
| Walk unlock            | ≤ 1.2 km to stop                                                  |
| Ojek feeder            | ≤ 8 km to stop                                                    |
| Interchange            | ≤ 600 m between real stops; never invent hubs                     |
| Pre-OSRM shortlist     | ≤ 28 plans                                                        |
| Near-cheapest band     | cheapest + Rp 5,000 → pick fastest                                |
| OSRM failure           | straight-line ~22 km/h fallback                                   |

## Change discipline

1. Prefer pure functions; mock OSRM at the enrichment boundary in unit tests.
2. Add/adjust goldens in `src/lib/__tests__/planner-goldens.test.ts` (G1–G9 covered; G10–G12 backlog — see `docs/TDD.md`).
3. Use tiny synthetic stop/network fixtures unless the case needs real corridor topology.
4. `/admin` traffic factors live in localStorage master only — not multi-tenant auth.
